# CR-23-L-1 red: the testlist loader accepted a manifest whose declared test is not the entry naming it
# The per-entry fcov check (gen_fcov.check_test) validates the manifest against the ENTRY NAME before it reads
# coverage, so a differing stem can only end as an unverifiable protocol error. The loader required the three-way
# equality for MEASURED entries only, so it accepted a wiring the check can never pass. Rule now: every entry that
# names a manifest names its own, or null. This withdraws the positive side of CM153-L-1.
# Taken on a detached archive of e754a83 (the current head), with gen_test_pmc_ctrl_pin_off's field already nulled,
# so the red is the new case alone rather than the eight reverted entries.
# Sections 1 and 2 are the redirected self-test output; section 3 is the rule against the COMMITTED testlist.
== 1. RED: the case added, the rule NOT yet written ==
   command: python3 dv/auto_dv/flow/gen_flow_util.py --self-test   (rc 2)
   SELF-TEST BAD load_testlist refuses an unmeasured entry whose fcov_expectation_file stem is another test's (CR-23-L-1: check_test validates against the entry name whether measured or not) (message names 'must be')
   SELF-TEST BAD build-input gate case 13: every listed non-input is tracked and each glob class matches a tracked file (['git ls-files failed: fatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).']); list sha256 80d4a7081e03
   ok cases in this run: 149

